1
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:21,370
you stop?

2
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:30,880
Shut it up!

3
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:37,800
What in the world is going on?

4
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,860
How did Luffy's crew find us?

5
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:41,632
And Law is here as well.

6
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:44,173
I was told that he had been apprehended.

7
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:47,431
You were handing me this instant cardinal!

8
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:51,917
I beautifully reported everything
to Lord Orochi, just like always.

9
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,529
What could have gone awry?

10
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:55,000
It can't be.

11
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:58,553
Did Lord Orochi not arrange
any countermeasures for this?

12
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:02,517
Do you really think a regular old
bomb would take down a ship like ours?

13
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,140
Not a chance in hell, bro!

14
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:07,180
The Sunny can cross a thousand seas!

15
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,917
It's made of wood from the Tree of Adam!

16
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,588
It won't go down that easy!

17
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:13,734
You got anything else?

18
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:16,586
Cause those weak-ass
bombs ain't gonna cut it!

19
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,157
So the sabotage wasn't enough?

20
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:22,740
Those sneaky scumbags couldn't
put a scratch on our ship.

21
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:26,040
The sails are another story, though.

22
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,440
Sorry we're late, Keen Aemon.

23
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:36,231
We had to patch up the sails,
and that took a little while.

24
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:38,869
Quite all right, though
it gave me a scare.

25
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,097
Hey, Keen!

26
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:42,460
Where is everybody?

27
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,737
I thought you were bringing backup.

28
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:47,177
I guess our original plans
kind of changed, huh?

29
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:50,580
Is it okay if we smash those
battleships to pieces then?

30
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:51,918
Yes, what happened?

31
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:55,657
I was under the impression we would
have lots of reinforcements here.

32
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:56,570
Yeah!

33
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:59,680
Where's 3,500 people from the labor camp?

34
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:02,080
Indeed, what's the status?

35
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:06,357
Where are the Yakuza, who are supposed
to be coming from all over the country?

36
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:08,675
Weren't there about 200 or so of them?

37
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:11,117
Something's not adding up.

38
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:14,080
Dogstorm had 200
musketeers at Hitachi Port,

39
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,965
and then the Atomiyama
Thieves Brigade had 280.

40
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:20,157
Yeah, and where are all
the ships we repaired?

41
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,397
There were dozens of them.

42
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:22,310
What happened?

43
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:26,357
And what about that supply of swords and
spears that was coming in from Ringo?

44
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:29,146
Without weapons for our
troops, we're screwed.

45
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:31,337
Hey, Kin'emon!

46
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:32,891
Know anything about this?

47
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,720
I confess, a substantial misstep was made.

48
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:52,380
My deepest apologies, Sir Luffy.

49
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:55,800
Regrettably, the entire plan was leaked.

50
00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:01,955
I wish I could tell you where the
others are, but I know nothing at all.

51
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:04,237
So that's the reason why nobody's here.

52
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:06,477
We should think about retreating, maybe.

53
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:07,480
No way!

54
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:08,960
That's messed up!

55
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:11,497
We don't know jack about what's going on.

56
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:14,837
In fact, we thought we sunk your
ship until just a second ago.

57
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:17,567
But we did sink all of
the ships at the dock.

58
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:19,797
You should have seen the port last night.

59
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:21,420
The Shogun was thorough.

60
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:24,133
He had us bombed the major bridges, too.

61
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:26,869
Now there's no passage
between the regions.

62
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,080
You get it, right?

63
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:33,053
There's not a chance in hell
anyone's coming to help you!

64
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:35,277
Even if they made it to the poor,

65
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:38,457
no one's going to be reaching
Onigashima without a boat!

66
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:42,481
And this was your last chance, the
only day the raid might succeed!

67
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,660
And by the way,

68
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:48,232
I heard we're going to start killing
all the rebels we rounded up tomorrow!

69
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,920
I almost forgot.

70
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:52,737
There's one last thing
we need to tell you.

71
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:54,080
Sorry about that.

72
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:57,280
Figured there's only so
much bad news you can take.

73
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,657
Bad news, you say?

74
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:01,917
That banquet we're having isn't
just for the Fire Festival.

75
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,588
It's much bigger than that.

76
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:07,137
It's a once-in-a-lifetime
celebration because the Beast

77
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:11,102
Pirates and the Big Mom Pirates
are forming the ultimate alliance!

78
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:15,040
You have got to be shitting me!

79
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,900
Two emperors teaming up?

80
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:21,197
We're unstoppable with both Commander
Daddy and Big Mom on our side.

81
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:24,077
No matter who you recruit,
you got nothing on us!

82
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:25,395
The worst generation?

83
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:26,497
Yeah, I'll say.

84
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:29,280
Sink him and get this over with already!

85
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,940
Now get ready to fire!

86
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:41,900
Meh, you're really full
of yourselves, huh?

87
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:44,180
Well, I'm sick of it!

88
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:45,880
Stand back, you guys!

89
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,200
You stand back.

90
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,029
Take your own dumb advice.

91
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:50,540
I got this, Drop!

92
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,917
Make yourself useful and stay out of it!

93
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,317
I said no, back off!

94
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:56,694
All right, ladies, stop your bickering.

95
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,440
I got this.

96
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,440
Hey, Jaggy, not you, too!

97
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:02,420
I doubt you're annoying!

98
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,620
Neither of you better
get in my way! Watch me!

99
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:07,280
I was here to watch!

100
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,600
Get back here!

101
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:10,640
I said I got that!

102
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,354
Oh, like hell, you do!

103
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,220
You back off! No way!

104
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:22,994
Room's even more effective in the rain.

105
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:23,990
No fair!

106
00:06:24,073 --> 00:06:25,137
Your power's too cool!

107
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:26,857
Why do you gotta go and rub it in?

108
00:06:26,940 --> 00:06:27,770
Suck it up.

109
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:30,077
You don't need to be a damn Chef!

110
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:31,837
Oh, the kettle has an opinion.

111
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:32,920
You're both dumb!

112
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,337
I can wrap this up in one shot, you know!

113
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:39,957
Once you shut up, I'll show I can do the
same damn thing in half the time as you!

114
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:41,158
We're wasting time.

115
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,377
I'm going in and you can't stop me.

116
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:44,695
You got that, losers?

117
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:46,430
Losers!

118
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:48,500
Now I'll kick your ass first!

119
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,477
Good, because I'll handle these guys!

120
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:51,390
You're ridiculous.

121
00:06:51,473 --> 00:06:53,040
Hey, you three!

122
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:55,437
Don't go thinking that
you'll leave here alive!

123
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:56,350
Shut up!

124
00:06:56,433 --> 00:06:57,377
You're beneath me!

125
00:06:57,460 --> 00:06:58,290
You shut up.

126
00:06:58,373 --> 00:07:00,240
I'll take care of him. Oh, yeah?

127
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:01,920
It's on now!

128
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:07,790
Rude!

129
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,720
Ah!

130
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:40,670
Ah! Ah!

131
00:07:40,753 --> 00:07:41,583
That's me!

132
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:43,030
Ah!

133
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:48,920
Ah!

134
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:50,330
Ah!

135
00:07:50,413 --> 00:07:51,243
Nice!

136
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:02,660
Injection shot!

137
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:36,820
See what I did there?

138
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:38,980
Who's the loser now, loser?

139
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,715
Let me make one thing perfectly clear.

140
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,200
I'm the one who sank that last ship.

141
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,920
I sank that thing, it was all me!

142
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,297
Get out of here with that!

143
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:50,500
You're taking credit for my work!

144
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:53,347
Wait, aren't those three
guys in an alliance?

145
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:58,600
Up ahead!

146
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,680
That's the Kyoshiro family ship!

147
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:04,820
Perfect timing, Kyoshiro!

148
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:06,920
We had nothing to fear!

149
00:09:07,760 --> 00:09:09,937
Seems you're in quite a bit of trouble!

150
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:11,785
We could really use some help!

151
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:15,277
The Shogun ordered for them to be
sunk to the bottom of the sea, bud!

152
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,577
You don't say.

153
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:18,780
Orders to sink the enemy, huh?

154
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,260
Allow me.

155
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:25,850
Boss!

156
00:09:25,933 --> 00:09:28,193
There's something you're not telling us!

157
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:38,077
I have no desire to sink you, so
I simply disabled the cannons!

158
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:40,237
you had aimed at the samurai's vessel.

159
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,300
I know him.

160
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:42,680
We fought before.

161
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,057
Careful with this one!

162
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:45,477
He's terrifying with a blade!

163
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:48,140
This man is one of the Shogun's lapdogs.

164
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:51,184
He's the Yakuza boss who
took over after Yoguro.

165
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:56,740
Greetings to you, Akazaya Samurai.

166
00:09:57,280 --> 00:10:00,560
I'm the reputable gangster
who runs the Flower Capital.

167
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:03,567
The people there know
me as Napping Kyoshiro.

168
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:06,160
My family's made up of 200 men.

169
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:09,260
Our swords are at your
disposal for the raid.

170
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,600
They're doing what now?

171
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:12,977
Are you joking, boss?

172
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:14,320
Explain yourself!

173
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:16,091
What favor do you owe us?

174
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:18,102
Do you not operate under Orochi?

175
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:25,820
My intent is to pay back the immeasurable
debt that I owe the Kozuki clan.

176
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:31,780
You have been in my
thoughts, King, for years.

177
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:33,720
You know me?

178
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:38,373
Do you recall when the Mountain God
charged into the capital 40 years ago?

179
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:43,957
The public believed that
the chaos was the result

180
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:47,477
of Lord Odin's antics But
they were wrong in that

181
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:51,117
assumption It was in fact
caused by you and your

182
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:54,640
ill-advised plan to get
rich by selling a young boar

183
00:10:59,100 --> 00:10:59,930
What?

184
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:03,360
But only one man knows
about what happened that day

185
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:08,099
Why do you think everyone
calls it the mountain god?

186
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:09,770
What?

187
00:11:09,853 --> 00:11:10,683
It's all my fault.

188
00:11:11,060 --> 00:11:13,560
The capital's doomed and it's my fault.

189
00:11:15,620 --> 00:11:16,977
No, don't tell me.

190
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:20,380
Is that you, Digital? You
can't be. It's really true?

191
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,757
It is I.

192
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:30,280
I suppose you wouldn't recognize me.

193
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:32,237
I wish to join you right away.

194
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:35,477
However, I determined it'd be
wiser to appear to be your enemy.

195
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:36,720
Just a bit longer.

196
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:39,480
Imagine if I revealed who I was.

197
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:44,480
The betrayer in your midst would have
relayed that to Orochi and had me killed.

198
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:47,250
Denjiro!

199
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:48,510
Silence, you!

200
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:52,357
Instead, I retained his
trust until the end,

201
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:57,460
and I liberated the 1,000 samurai
locked in the Rasetsu prison quarters.

202
00:11:58,060 --> 00:11:59,295
There are more ships?

203
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:00,780
Enemy reinforcements.

204
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:06,280
You can add 1,200 soldiers to the total.

205
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:16,097
We've been waiting for this day, and
we're ready to fight with all we've got!

206
00:12:16,180 --> 00:12:20,121
Since when has boss killed Shura
one of the damned Akazaya Samurai?

207
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:24,060
Going for Morigashima before
it's too late! Yes, sir!

208
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,240
It's really you!

209
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:34,940
Commendable work, Keen.

210
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:37,877
I knew you were sharp,
but I must hand it to you.

211
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:41,254
You understood Lord Yasui's
message and adapted quickly.

212
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:44,560
Two birds of flame to represent time.

213
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,040
A Habu Viper to indicate location.

214
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:50,674
And a reversed crescent moon,
which signifies rebellion.

215
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:54,635
Twilight, the second hour of
the Bird at Fire Festival.

216
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:56,940
It shall take place at Habu Port.

217
00:12:57,240 --> 00:13:00,160
The initial symbol did
not have those two lines.

218
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,946
That was the one that
Orochi got his hands on.

219
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:10,500
Before his death, Lord Yasui
altered it and helped get word out.

220
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:15,117
Obviously, the newly added lines
going through the serpent's stomachs.

221
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:18,457
instruct the reader to remove
the midsection of the word.

222
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:23,300
So without the letters in the center,
Habu Port, also called Habu Monda,

223
00:13:23,580 --> 00:13:24,720
becomes Head!

224
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,340
It means wharf.

225
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:33,835
Lord Yasui always did love the view
of the maple tree forest from there.

226
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:35,970
Huh?

227
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:40,157
Even though it was a simple message,

228
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,181
you deliberately misinterpreted
it when you spoke!

229
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,937
Sensing there was a
spy amongst your group,

230
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:50,961
you pretended to direct
your associates elsewhere!

231
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:54,534
But you knew they were wise
enough to discern the truth!

232
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:56,600
At any rate, the point is,

233
00:13:56,820 --> 00:13:59,877
each of these ports is associated
with a particular animal.

234
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:04,437
With the moment's consideration, the image
of a lizard will likely come to mind.

235
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:06,520
Thus, Tokage Port in Udon.

236
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:12,840
Thinking back, that symbol
never did look like a lizard.

237
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:17,017
I had no reason to question it
because Master Keen was so confident.

238
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:21,700
The unwitting spy passed a long word at
the false rendezvous point to Orochi.

239
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:24,420
Just as you planned, Master Keen.

240
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:30,237
Such is the foolishness of a man
who did as he pleased for too long.

241
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:35,320
Orochi misjudged the distance between
locations and waited until last night to act!

242
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:37,277
By the time they began their assault,

243
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:40,017
all of your allied forces had
already crossed the bridges,

244
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:42,457
and the ships you needed
had left the port!

245
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:45,360
The ones they sank were
those few left behind.

246
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:50,580
So according to your plan, the
4,200 troops concealed themselves.

247
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:55,138
They laid in wait within the Maple
Forest near the wharf at Habu Port.

248
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:57,660
You mean they're still alive?

249
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:18,360
It may be 20 years later, but I still
remember Lord Odin's legendary death.

250
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:22,360
We've lived every day believing
the Kozuki clan would return.

251
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:25,620
Hakusaya 9, let us fight together.

252
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:28,180
We are here to aid you.

253
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:34,800
The plan to raid Onigashima
hasn't missed a single step.

254
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:42,940
Combine our 1,200 soldiers with your
troops and you now stand at 5,400 strong!

255
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:49,640
Onward to the banquet!

256
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,360
Would you look at that!

257
00:15:56,020 --> 00:15:59,737
I don't really follow what happened,
but it looks like everything worked out.

258
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:01,700
There's too many of them!

259
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:03,857
Things aren't looking good for us!

260
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:05,540
Any news from Onigashima?

261
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:07,217
Can't get a hold of them!

262
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:10,535
I bet they're preoccupied
with the big party right now!

263
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:14,320
So my efforts were all
for naught in the end!

264
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,840
Damn you, Kin'emon!

265
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:19,670
Bravo!

266
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:21,020
As expected,

267
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:25,454
you have risen to the occasion and
proven to be quite the capable leader!

268
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,940
Yes, Worf, of course.

269
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:43,120
Not Tokage Port.

270
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:56,460
You, Gar, can be honest with
us, Kin'emon. No offense,

271
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:59,717
but we've known you long enough to know
that a plan like this is not within

272
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:05,337
your skill set just admit you made a
mistake and we won't be angry stop it.

273
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:09,117
You thought the message was
tokage you cannot fool me.

274
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:11,877
I said stop it at least
the mistake settled in

275
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:17,997
our favor what a happy
accident to be honest.

276
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:20,417
I fear that i might perish
in the battle ahead.

277
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:24,017
I did just use up a whole lifetime's

278
00:17:24,100 --> 00:17:28,257
worth of luck after all i can scarcely.

279
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,575
I disagree with that.

280
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:30,800
Master Kin'emon!

281
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,829
We'll follow you anywhere!

282
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:37,884
Though if you are lucky, then we are lucky
to have you at our side in this battle.

283
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:46,297
And even if you do die out there, at the
very least we will all die beside you.

284
00:17:46,380 --> 00:17:49,297
We serve Lord Odin together
and will avenge him together.

285
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:53,037
We may have come from different worlds,
but we are comrades in arms now.

286
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:53,950
To the end.

287
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:05,800
Such pleasantries from scoundrels
like you hardly comforting.

288
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:10,697
Hold up your sword with pride, keen!

289
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:13,368
We shall claim victory
in the opening fight.

290
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:20,997
Win or lose, I'm prepared.

291
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:25,380
We will avenge Lord Odin; the time is now!

292
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,666
You have our full support,
no matter the cost!

293
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:39,060
Never mind, Kin'emon.

294
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:41,197
I must make haste to Onigashima.

295
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:44,809
The role assigned to be by Lord
Orochi is still unfulfilled.

296
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:48,240
There's one thing I have left to do.

297
00:18:58,060 --> 00:19:00,960
Anjirou, you won't take Lord Momonosuke!

298
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,180
What will that do?

299
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:09,060
I am on my way! Stop it!

300
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:11,237
You'll drown if you jump into the sea!

301
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:15,020
You would trample our dreams
and get us with a smile!

302
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:17,060
You bastard!

303
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:21,500
I admit, I do find
pleasure in this moment.

304
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:25,677
Sabotage, duplicity, betrayal
with a surprise ending.

305
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:28,348
What a complex role I
had the honor to play.

306
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:33,680
And speaking of roles, thank you
all so much for playing the fool.

307
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:38,670
KONTINO!

308
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:48,453
What better way to end the play than
to stain the stage with Kozuki blood?

309
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,360
Kawamatsu, help!

310
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:58,800
Lord Momonosuke!

311
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:01,540
Don't you worry, Momonosuke.

312
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,957
I'll let your sister
follow you into death.

313
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:05,497
You hear that, Kawamatsu?

314
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:07,900
I will find Hiyori and slay her, too.

315
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:11,060
You fools confirm she's alive after all.

316
00:20:14,140 --> 00:20:15,660
Damn you, Kanjuro!

317
00:20:16,140 --> 00:20:18,846
That crane you painted
is flying immaculately!

318
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,197
What of the monstrosities you made us?

319
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:22,960
They washed away with water!

320
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:25,580
I thought you lacked talent! Huh?

321
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:26,920
It's too high!

322
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:29,797
Someone please get me
down from here, please!

323
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:32,760
I don't want to die! Kanjuro? Momo?

324
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:35,320
Wait, where are you going?

325
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:37,874
This is the last you'll ever see of me!

326
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,320
This is only a fraction
of Commander Taito's army.

327
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:47,460
You'll be dead before
you ever reach the shore.

328
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:53,900
Someone help me!

329
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,900
Let him go!

330
00:20:58,340 --> 00:20:59,660
Lord Momonosuke, no!

331
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:02,844
You'll pay for betraying
the Akazaya 9, Kanjuro!

332
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:04,617
Stay strong, Lord Momonosuke!

333
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:05,700
This is terrible!

334
00:21:06,940 --> 00:21:07,770
Damn.

335
00:21:07,853 --> 00:21:10,077
So the whole plan nearly
fell apart because

336
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:12,537
Kanjuro's been feeding info to the enemy?

337
00:21:12,620 --> 00:21:13,700
So it would seem.

338
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:15,660
We better save Momo quick.

339
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:18,330
On it.

340
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:25,300
Hey, Reef!

341
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:28,720
It turns out Kanjuro is
actually an enemy spy!

342
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:32,400
He's taking Momo away right now! Huh?

343
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:33,480
Are you sure?

344
00:21:33,820 --> 00:21:34,700
No way!

345
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:37,762
He fooled us all this time
and nobody had a clue!

346
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:40,660
What a jerk!

347
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:46,680
We can't let that bastard get away!

348
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:48,488
I'll try to shoot him down!

349
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:51,220
Special attack!

350
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,280
Green Star Platinus!

351
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:54,720
Shoot him in!

352
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:02,980
A valiant effort, but not enough!

353
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:06,181
I don't have time to
entertain imbeciles like you!

354
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,400
What's that cloud?

355
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:22,340
I have a bad feeling
about this, Sir Sanji.

356
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,060
Turn back immediately.

357
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:26,260
Clouds, clouds.

358
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:29,517
Whatever technique he's doing,
I've never seen it before.

359
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:30,800
Ink clouds.

360
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,037
Ink arrows.

361
00:22:36,120 --> 00:22:37,460
Fall like rain.

362
00:22:45,860 --> 00:22:49,140
Ukiyo Portrait, evening shower.

363
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:57,320
It's dangerous here!

364
00:22:57,580 --> 00:22:59,286
Turn the boat around quickly!

365
00:23:03,120 --> 00:23:04,440
I need help! Nami!

366
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:10,697
only one man's allowed
to shoot an arrow through

367
00:23:10,780 --> 00:23:14,240
nami and robin's heart
figuratively and that man is me

368
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:22,577
i am begging you to
please stop this Kanjuro

369
00:23:22,660 --> 00:23:25,340
you are going to kill
every last one of them

370
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:32,160
that i shall and rightfully
so it's their time

371
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,940
Your father, Rodin,

372
00:23:36,260 --> 00:23:37,497
and your mother, Toki,

373
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:39,617
dangled a false hope
in front of those poor

374
00:23:39,700 --> 00:23:42,171
fools by delaying their inevitable deaths.

375
00:23:42,880 --> 00:23:47,600
Now, twenty years later, their
execution must be completed at last.

376
00:23:49,860 --> 00:23:50,690
Frankly,

377
00:23:50,773 --> 00:23:53,557
it would be a mercy since
those foolish samurai are

378
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:56,157
now serving under a cowardly
little imp like yourself.

379
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:59,797
You are nothing but an
imprudent child lacking in

380
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:03,056
conviction and whimpering
at the first sign of danger.

381
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,617
You can cry but I will laugh!

382
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:12,480
What am I to say?

383
00:24:15,580 --> 00:24:22,540
I know best of all that I'm no Kozuki Onion
For how can I ever hope to measure up?

384
00:24:26,780 --> 00:24:29,460
What am I supposed to do? I'm helpless!

385
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:38,228
Are you certain that's
what you want to say?

386
00:24:38,680 --> 00:24:42,080
If you tell them that, no
one will come to your aid.

387
00:24:45,120 --> 00:24:45,950
But...

388
00:24:53,300 --> 00:24:54,130
Everyone!

389
00:24:54,213 --> 00:24:55,800
Can you hear me?

390
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:01,060
That's Lord Momonosuke

391
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:05,680
I ask you that you do not
worry about my well-being

392
00:25:07,420 --> 00:25:11,020
That is exactly what the
enemy wants you to do

393
00:25:12,700 --> 00:25:14,340
I promise to you,

394
00:25:14,660 --> 00:25:18,857
I shall escape all on my own You
must defeat Conney and Orochi

395
00:25:18,940 --> 00:25:22,900
without me Please find a way
to protect the land of Moro

396
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:32,377
Such noble words from the
young lord It stirs my

397
00:25:32,460 --> 00:25:35,640
heart to hear them How brave
you've turned out to be

398
00:25:37,580 --> 00:25:43,820
We all put our faith in you That
was pretty manly Nice job, Momo

399
00:25:46,620 --> 00:25:47,980
Hey, Momo

400
00:25:49,340 --> 00:25:51,220
It's okay, I know

401
00:25:51,780 --> 00:25:54,740
You're just a little
crybaby with a dumb Totknot!

402
00:25:55,120 --> 00:25:56,826
What are you gonna do anyway?

403
00:25:57,200 --> 00:25:58,906
Nothing, and you know it too!

404
00:25:59,120 --> 00:26:01,002
How could you be so rude to him?

405
00:26:01,100 --> 00:26:02,317
You better take that back!

406
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:03,694
Who's this guy anyway?

407
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:04,880
I'll chop him up!

408
00:26:05,220 --> 00:26:07,320
Gotta find a way to survive, okay?

409
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:10,700
Just hang on, and we'll come rescue you!

410
00:26:15,020 --> 00:26:16,560
Because you're my friend.

411
00:26:21,220 --> 00:26:22,050
Oh!

412
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:26,710
Oh!

413
00:26:28,100 --> 00:26:28,930
Oh! Oh!

414
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:30,750
Oh!

415
00:26:33,280 --> 00:26:34,520
Oh!

416
00:26:35,620 --> 00:26:36,450
Oh!

417
00:26:36,533 --> 00:26:37,363
Oh! Oh!

418
00:26:37,880 --> 00:26:38,710
Oh!

419
00:26:39,220 --> 00:26:40,050
Oh!

420
00:26:40,133 --> 00:26:40,963
Okay!

421
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:47,280
Off to Onigashima! Yeah!

422
00:27:05,480 --> 00:27:06,310
Luffy!

423
00:27:06,393 --> 00:27:08,452
One of the enemy's ships is getting away!

424
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:11,537
Just let it go!

425
00:27:11,620 --> 00:27:13,977
They're all heading in
the same direction anyway.

426
00:27:14,060 --> 00:27:15,413
We can sink them later.

427
00:27:16,520 --> 00:27:17,350
Huh?

428
00:27:17,580 --> 00:27:19,257
Hey, wasn't there another ship?

429
00:27:19,340 --> 00:27:20,170
There was.

430
00:27:20,253 --> 00:27:21,400
Then I sunk it.

431
00:27:24,660 --> 00:27:26,600
Master King, forgive me.

432
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:29,000
I failed to protect him.

433
00:27:29,180 --> 00:27:30,037
You are alive.

434
00:27:30,120 --> 00:27:31,077
Then that's enough.

435
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:34,513
I doubt they will take Ward
Momonosuke's life right away.

436
00:27:36,200 --> 00:27:37,337
One question, though.

437
00:27:37,420 --> 00:27:38,497
Your face!

438
00:27:38,580 --> 00:27:40,520
How did it transform so?

439
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:45,320
A tale for another time.

440
00:27:47,600 --> 00:27:49,540
It is good to see you.

441
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:51,840
Is everyone all right?

442
00:27:52,040 --> 00:27:52,980
Who needs help?

443
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:57,120
We have a few injuries and
some ships in need of repair.

444
00:27:57,660 --> 00:28:00,377
I appreciate it, but I'll
just head for the island.

445
00:28:00,460 --> 00:28:03,120
I didn't come this far just to die at sea.

446
00:28:03,820 --> 00:28:08,680
Hey, my ship is not your
personal samurai garrison.

447
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:20,477
I said you're not welcome
here pack it up then make

448
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:23,460
sure the Straw Hats don't
hog all the glory Yeah!

449
00:28:30,260 --> 00:28:31,520
What was that?

450
00:28:31,700 --> 00:28:32,641
Oh, he's firing!

451
00:28:34,780 --> 00:28:36,620
It's the ship that got away!

452
00:28:38,340 --> 00:28:39,680
On-range cannon?

453
00:28:39,980 --> 00:28:42,837
They can still hit us from
all the way over there!

454
00:28:42,920 --> 00:28:46,391
So they weren't running away,
they were just repositioning!

455
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:52,777
These are our high precision cannons.

456
00:28:52,860 --> 00:28:54,297
The best in Wano.

457
00:28:54,380 --> 00:28:58,797
We got weapons factories all over the
country pumping these bad boys out.

458
00:28:58,880 --> 00:29:03,237
And if these don't do the job, we have
plenty of other ways to blow you up!

459
00:29:03,320 --> 00:29:05,017
Why don't you come at us?

460
00:29:05,100 --> 00:29:06,337
Show us what you got.

461
00:29:06,420 --> 00:29:07,800
Are you scared?

462
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:14,780
Hold the ship back!

463
00:29:15,020 --> 00:29:17,020
Those shots can save us from here!

464
00:29:27,660 --> 00:29:28,500
Damn it.

465
00:29:28,760 --> 00:29:31,936
I thought it was weird that
they fled without a fight.

466
00:29:33,500 --> 00:29:34,840
Full speed ahead!

467
00:29:35,160 --> 00:29:36,580
We gotta get closer!

468
00:29:39,780 --> 00:29:44,160
I don't care how many samurai ships
sink as long as we make it there.

469
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:52,160
Damn it.

470
00:29:52,460 --> 00:29:54,636
We can't let them keep this distance.

471
00:29:55,680 --> 00:29:56,740
We'll sink.

472
00:29:56,980 --> 00:29:58,340
We must close the gap.

473
00:30:04,740 --> 00:30:06,877
Seems this battle's already over.

474
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:09,440
We're untouchable from back here!

475
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:22,320
Now fire! Fire!

476
00:30:27,220 --> 00:30:29,380
Fishman Caracal!

477
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:31,780
Spill it away!

478
00:30:51,160 --> 00:30:52,160
Oh, crap!

479
00:30:52,420 --> 00:30:54,057
There's a huge hole in the ship!

480
00:30:54,140 --> 00:30:54,970
It's falling!

481
00:31:01,620 --> 00:31:02,780
Fishback karate!

482
00:31:04,100 --> 00:31:06,380
Spear wave for a summer!

483
00:31:19,220 --> 00:31:21,749
That guy just destroyed
all of our cannons!

484
00:31:25,140 --> 00:31:27,097
Something is happening over there.

485
00:31:27,180 --> 00:31:28,917
What if a child drowned at sea?

486
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:30,657
And came back as a vengeful ghost!

487
00:31:30,740 --> 00:31:32,037
intent on killing them all?

488
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:32,950
No!

489
00:31:33,360 --> 00:31:35,317
You got the vengeful part right.

490
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:37,120
Wait, but what was that?

491
00:31:46,060 --> 00:31:48,240
I think somebody's down there.

492
00:31:51,920 --> 00:31:54,720
Everyone, if I may have a word.

493
00:31:57,380 --> 00:32:02,137
I hail from the Fishman
District of the Ryugu Kingdom.

494
00:32:02,220 --> 00:32:06,660
A place beneath the waves for
those bold enough to seek passage.

495
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:13,140
My apologies for the trouble
I may have caused you,

496
00:32:13,460 --> 00:32:15,872
especially seeing that I'm a new recruit.

497
00:32:15,980 --> 00:32:19,237
But I have ventured here
today to share a ceremonial

498
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:22,580
cup of sake with the boss of
the Straw Hat Pirate Crew.

499
00:32:23,220 --> 00:32:24,940
If you'll have me, that is.

500
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:31,880
I'm known as

501
00:32:32,600 --> 00:32:35,180
First son of the sea, Jinbei

502
00:32:38,700 --> 00:32:40,020
Are you kidding?

503
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:43,520
He is seriously going
to join the Straw Huts.

504
00:32:44,740 --> 00:32:46,477
It hasn't been long.

505
00:32:46,560 --> 00:32:48,337
So I'm certain you'll remember me!

506
00:32:48,420 --> 00:32:51,460
Now let's make this official, shall we?

507
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:55,770
Ah!

508
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:00,390
Jinbei!

509
00:33:01,420 --> 00:33:02,250
Jinbei!

510
00:33:02,333 --> 00:33:03,500
It's Jinbei!

511
00:33:06,600 --> 00:33:10,306
So sorry to keep you waiting,
but I thank you for indulging me.

512
00:33:10,800 --> 00:33:14,520
Luffy, I have come back
alive just as I promised.

513
00:33:15,040 --> 00:33:17,860
Glad I made it back in
time for the big battle.

514
00:33:24,940 --> 00:33:26,380
We'll be back.
